Relay the OAuth callback into the app with an intent:// navigation.

callback.html hands the result back by writing to localStorage, which the
workbench then reads. That never happens here: the callback lands in the system
browser while the workbench runs in a WebView, and the two are separate storage
origins, so every sign-in flow hangs waiting for a value that was written
somewhere else.

intent:// rather than a custom scheme, because Chrome refuses to navigate to one
from script without a user gesture while intent:// is always permitted and
resolves through the manifest intent-filter. Synchronously rather than from a
timeout, because the activation that permits the navigation is gone by the time
one would fire. The localStorage write is left in place so the flow still works
if the page is ever opened in the WebView itself.

diff --git a/src/vs/code/browser/workbench/callback.html b/src/vs/code/browser/workbench/callback.html
index 4f54d4d..abdefec 100644
--- a/src/vs/code/browser/workbench/callback.html
+++ b/src/vs/code/browser/workbench/callback.html
@@ -62,6 +62,22 @@
 			}
 
 			localStorage.setItem(`vscode-web.url-callbacks[${id}]`, JSON.stringify(uri));
+
+			// Relay the callback into the Android app.
+			//
+			// The localStorage write above is how the workbench normally collects this,
+			// and it never reaches us: the callback lands in the system browser while the
+			// workbench runs in a WebView, and those are separate storage origins.
+			//
+			// intent:// rather than a custom scheme, because Chrome blocks navigation to
+			// one from script without a user gesture while intent:// is always allowed and
+			// resolves through the manifest intent-filter. Synchronous rather than
+			// deferred, because the activation permitting the navigation is gone by the
+			// time a timeout would fire.
+			try {
+				const payload = encodeURIComponent(JSON.stringify({ id: id, uri: uri }));
+				window.location.href = 'intent://callback?data=' + payload + '#Intent;scheme=vscodroid;end';
+			} catch (e) { }
 		</script>
 
 		<!-- Styling -->
